sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-glue-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "How many heads a planarian cellular collective produces is not directly encoded in its genome, since the same wild-type cells can produce 1-, 2- or 0-headed planaria depending on their history; the genome encodes the hardware (e.g. ion channels) while the outcome results from experience-sensitive electrophysiological 'software'.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Planarian head number is not directly encoded in the genome";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Bioelectric networks: the cognitive glue enabling evolutionary scaling from physiology to mind”, Animal cognition (2023), doi:10.1007/s10071-023-01780-3; section “Basal cognition without neurons: what dynamic bodies think about › Re-writing morphogenetic memories: ontogenetic and evolutionary timescales”. Scope: Planarian flatworms"
}
